EXAMPLES=[]
def ex(n,q,steps,answer,pages):
 EXAMPLES.append({'id':'we-5-source-'+str(n),'num':str(n),'title':'Example '+str(n),'problem':q,'given':'The printed vector functions and parameter values.','method':'Apply component derivatives and keep scalar/vector products distinct.','steps':steps,'answer':answer,'progressiveSolution':True,'solutionOrigin':'SpaceBook learning enhancement','sourceReferences':[{'pageStart':min(pages),'pageEnd':max(pages),'verification':'all components and source working compared with JPG/PDF'}]})
ex(8,'Verify (F⃗×G⃗)′ = F⃗′×G⃗ + F⃗×G⃗′ for F⃗ = î+tĵ+t²k̂, G⃗ = tî+eᵗĵ+3k̂.',['Compute the ordered cross product: F⃗×G⃗ = (3t−t²eᵗ)î+(t³−3)ĵ+(eᵗ−t²)k̂.','Differentiate each component to obtain (3−2teᵗ−t²eᵗ)î+3t²ĵ+(eᵗ−2t)k̂.','Independently, F⃗′ = ĵ+2tk̂ and G⃗′ = î+eᵗĵ.','The first product is F⃗′×G⃗ = (3−2teᵗ)î+2t²ĵ−tk̂.','The second product is F⃗×G⃗′ = −t²eᵗî+t²ĵ+(eᵗ−t)k̂.','Add the products: (3−2teᵗ−t²eᵗ)î+3t²ĵ+(eᵗ−2t)k̂.','Both independently computed sides agree for all real t, proving this example. Factor order is essential because the cross product changes sign when reversed.'],'Both sides equal (3−2teᵗ−t²eᵗ)î+3t²ĵ+(eᵗ−2t)k̂.',[136,137])
ex(9,'For F⃗ = î+eᵗĵ+t²k̂, G⃗ = 3t²î+e⁻ᵗĵ−2tk̂, differentiate (a) 2F⃗+t³G⃗; (b) F⃗·G⃗.',['(a) Expand first: 2F⃗+t³G⃗ = (2+3t⁵)î+(2eᵗ+t³e⁻ᵗ)ĵ+(2t²−2t⁴)k̂.','The î coefficient differentiates to 15t⁴.','For the ĵ coefficient, use the product rule: (t³e⁻ᵗ)′ = 3t²e⁻ᵗ−t³e⁻ᵗ.','The k̂ coefficient differentiates to 4t−8t³.','Thus (a) is 15t⁴î+[2eᵗ+t²e⁻ᵗ(3−t)]ĵ+4t(1−2t²)k̂.','(b) Multiply corresponding components and sum: F⃗·G⃗ = 3t²+eᵗe⁻ᵗ−2t³ = 3t²+1−2t³.','Differentiate this scalar: 6t−6t². The unused h(t) in the printed introduction does not enter either requested derivative.'],'(a) 15t⁴î+[2eᵗ+t²e⁻ᵗ(3−t)]ĵ+4t(1−2t²)k̂; (b) 6t−6t².',[137])
ex(10,'Find velocity for r⃗(t) = 5tî+4tĵ−cos t k̂.',['Velocity is the derivative of the position vector.','The î component is 5t, with derivative 5.','The ĵ component is 4t, with derivative 4.','The k̂ component is −cos t, whose derivative is +sin t in radians.','Keep each component on its original fixed basis vector.','Combine: v⃗(t) = 5î+4ĵ+sin t k̂.','This vector is defined for all real t; its speed, if requested, would be √(41+sin²t).'],'5î+4ĵ+sin t k̂.',[137,138])
ex(11,'Find acceleration for r⃗(t) = (3t²+5)î−(4t²+2t−1)ĵ+sin t k̂.',['Acceleration is the second derivative of position.','First differentiate the î component: 3t²+5 gives 6t.','First differentiate the negative ĵ component: −4t²−2t+1 gives −8t−2.','First differentiate the k̂ component: sin t gives cos t.','Thus velocity is 6tî−(8t+2)ĵ+cos t k̂.','Differentiate once more: the component derivatives are 6,−8,−sin t.','Therefore a⃗(t) = 6î−8ĵ−sin t k̂, for all real t.'],'6î−8ĵ−sin t k̂.',[138])
ex(12,'Find speed after 30 seconds for r⃗(t) = 3tî+4ĵ+sin t k̂.',['Differentiate position using radian trigonometric calculus.','The component derivatives are 3,0,cos t; hence v⃗(t) = 3î+cos t k̂.','Speed is the magnitude, so s(t) = √(9+cos²t).','At 30 seconds with the printed sin t, use 30 radians: cos 30 ≈ 0.1542514499.','Therefore s(30) ≈ 3.003962967 m/s, or 3.00 m/s to two decimals.','The source instead sets cos 30 to √3/2, the cosine of 30 degrees, producing √39/2 ≈ 3.12 m/s.','These angle conventions cannot be mixed: replacing sin t by sin(πt/180) would require velocity coefficient (π/180)cos(πt/180), rather than simply cos t.'],'Radian-consistent speed √(9+cos²30) ≈ 3.003962967 m/s; printed degree substitution gives √39/2 ≈ 3.12 m/s.',[138])

